# Image pins for the "image" deploy mode (AI_ENGINE_DEPLOY_MODE=image).
# Copy to src/.env.images on the VPS (that path is git-ignored) and edit.
#
# CI (platform-infra build-push.yaml) publishes, for each build:
#   ghcr.io/axiomnode/ai-engine-api:<8-char tag>   plus the mutable :dev / :stg tags
#   ghcr.io/axiomnode/ai-engine-stats:<8-char tag> plus the mutable :dev / :stg tags
# The 8-char tag is the first 8 characters of the commit SHA of the platform-infra
# workflow run that built the image (shown in that run's "Build and push" step),
# NOT of an ai-engine commit.
#
# Prefer an immutable reference so a deploy is reproducible and rollback is a
# one-line edit:
#   AI_ENGINE_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/axiomnode/ai-engine-api@sha256:<digest>
# Tags work too. The mutable :stg / :dev tags make every `docker compose pull`
# move to whatever CI built last, which is exactly the drift pinning avoids.
AI_ENGINE_API_IMAGE=ghcr.io/axiomnode/ai-engine-api:REPLACE_WITH_TAG_OR_DIGEST
AI_ENGINE_STATS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/axiomnode/ai-engine-stats:REPLACE_WITH_TAG_OR_DIGEST
